  ],
  "text": "The word robot comes from a play written in nineteen twenty, and it means forced labour. But things that moved by themselves existed for thousands of years before the word did. Greek and Chinese engineers built clocks with figures that struck a bell on the hour. Al-Jazari built machines in the twelve hundreds that could be reset to play different rhythms. That is a programmable device, six hundred years before anyone used the word program. In seventeen thirty nine Vaucanson built a mechanical duck that appeared to eat and digest. It was a trick, and crowds paid to watch it, which is the point. Motion was never the hard part. The first industrial arm went into a factory in nineteen sixty one, lifting hot metal. It could not see anything at all. It repeated one movement, exactly, forever. What changed recently was never movement. It was the ability to notice and adapt. One of these every day. Follow so you do not miss tomorrow.",
  "voice": "802e3bc2b27e49c2995d23ef70e6ac89",
  "model": "s2.1-pro-free"
}
